0..53 Comment "//! Polymorphic lists support length, append and map."
54..119 Comment "//! The list is the polymorphic list of Martin-Löf\'s type theory"
120..168 Comment "//! [MartinLof-1984-intuitionistic_type_theory]."
169..172 Comment "//!"
173..227 Comment "//! An arm can return a call result or elide `return`."
228..275 Comment "//! It can nest the call under its constructor."
276..314 Comment "//! A fold can infer its element type."
315..318 Comment "//!"
319..364 Comment "//! Each structural call uses a smaller list."
365..428 Comment "//! The recursive natural-list source instantiates these folds."
429..432 Comment "//!"
433..489 Comment "//! - cites: [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]"
490..546 Comment "//! - cites: [MartinLof-1984-intuitionistic_type_theory]"
547..550 Comment "//!"
551..675 Comment "//! [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]: https://doi.org/10.1051/ita:2004015 \"Abel, Termination checking with types\""
676..848 Comment "//! [MartinLof-1984-intuitionistic_type_theory]: https://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/Bibliopolis-Book-retypeset-1984.pdf \"Martin-Löf, Intuitionistic Type Theory\""
